## Lore

The Coalition Commando is a combat specialist trained to serve in elite strike
forces and counter-insurgent and counter-terrorist teams, carrying out surgical
strikes, seek and destroy, sabotage, rescue and reconnaissance. Commandos are not
usually front-line troops, though they can be sent there and hold up well in a
straight firefight. They can pilot most CS power armor, the SAMAS included.

They serve under Coalition military specialists, often on long-range patrols and
strikes beyond the borders, and also in reaction units that put down uprisings
and other threats inside the States.

## GM Notes

**On assignment:** any body armor, 2D4 hand grenades, 1D4 smoke grenades, 1D4
flares, explosives if demolitions is known and the mission needs them, any
weapons, extra ammunition, optics, cameras and surveillance gear, and weeks of
rations. Commando squads may be issued non-regulation weapons, armor, gear and
vehicles for disguise and infiltration. What they actually get depends on the
mission, the commanding officer and what the base has.

Most have medium security clearance; trusted veterans have top clearance.
Quarters are the same as the Elite RPA''s, and room, board and basics are free.
Most commandos (60%) eventually carry 1D4+2 implants, and a quarter end up with
as many systems as a Headhunter.

Hand to Hand: Commando is taught only to Commandos and Special Forces.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'cs-commando');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'cs-commando';

